    if not row:\\n                continue\\n            if len(row) != width:\\n                raise ValueError(\"wrong number of cells in data row\")\\n\\n            sku = row[indices[\"sku\"]].strip()\\n            if not sku:\\n                raise ValueError(\"empty sku\")\\n\\n            quantity_text = row[indices[\"quantity\"]].strip()\\n            if not _INTEGER.match(quantity_text):\\n                raise ValueError(\"invalid quantity: %r\" % (quantity_text,))\\n            quantity = int(quantity_text)\\n\\n            price_text = row[indices[\"unit_price\"]].strip()\\n            try:\\n                price = Decimal(price_text)\\n            except Exception:\\n                raise ValueError(\"invalid unit price: %r\" % (price_text,)) from None\\n            if not price.is_finite() or price < 0:\\n                raise ValueError(\"invalid unit price: %r\" % (price_text,))\\n\\n            revenue = price * quantity\\n            if sku in revenues:\\n                quantities[sku] += quantity\\n                revenues[sku] += revenue\\n            else:\\n                quantities[sku] = quantity\\n                revenues[sku] = revenue\\n                order.append(sku)\\n\\n        summary = []\\n        for sku in order:\\n            total = revenues[sku].quantize(_CENT, rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\\n            if total == 0:\\n                total = Decimal(\"0.00\")\\n            summary.append({\\n                \"sku\": sku,\\n                \"quantity\": quantities[sku],\\n                \"revenue\": str(total),\\n            })\\n    return summary\\n'}</result>\n```\n\nThought: The file looks syntactically complete and implements the requirements. But I should carefully test edge cases before running pytest. Potential issues:\n\n1. CSV parsing: Using `csv.reader(io.StringIO(text, newline=\"\"), strict=True)`. `io.StringIO(text, newline=\"\")` preserves line endings, good. Blank physical lines ignored by csv, csv.reader yi